  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: House of Cards. Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "House of Cards is a dual-purpose term. While it commonly refers to the physical act of building towers with playing cards, it is also a specific, traditional drawing and building game. In its game form, players compete to build virtual 'rooms' and 'stories' by matching colors and ranks to score points based on triangle formations.",
    objective: 'Score the most points by forming specific geometric patterns (triangles) using your assigned color.',
    gameplay: "1. Players take turns placing cards on the table to 'build' a house.\n2. **Valleys**: Two cards placed side-by-side on the base.\n3. **Floors**: A horizontal card placed over a 'valley'.\n4. **Peaks (Triangles)**: Two cards leaning against each other over a floor.\n5. Points are awarded when a triangle is closed. If the majority of cards in a specific 'story' or triangle are of your color, you score the face value of those cards.",
    keyRules: [
      'Build from base: valleys (two cards side-by-side), then floors (horizontal over a valley), then peaks (two cards leaning over a floor).',
      'When a triangle is closed, the player whose color holds the majority in that story scores the face value of those cards.',
      'Players take turns placing one card at a time to extend the structure.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Two players. Each player is assigned a color (Red or Black) in the common half-deck variant; with the full deck both take turns placing cards to build the shared house structure.',
      deck: 'Standard 52-card deck. Often split by color (Red vs Black).',
      equipment: 'Standard 52-card deck. Often split by color (Red vs Black).',
      dealing: "Players draw cards to their hand (usually 3 at a time) to build their 'house'.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. Players take turns placing cards on the table to 'build' a house.\n2. **Valleys**: Two cards placed side-by-side on the base.\n3. **Floors**: A horizontal card placed over a 'valley'.\n4. **Peaks (Triangles)**: Two cards leaning against each other over a floor.\n5. Points are awarded when a triangle is closed. If the majority of cards in a specific 'story' or triangle are of your color, you score the face value of those cards.",
